   "grounded": false,
   "answer": "imagine market makers are running an ice cream stand. when they sell people options calls or puts, they have to buy or sell the actual stock behind the scenes so they don't get blown up if the price moves. \n\ngamma exposure (gex) is just the speed limit on how fast those market makers have to scramble to hedge. \n\nif dealer gamma is **positive**, they are basically speed bumps\u2014they sell when the market spikes and buy when it dips, which keeps everything calm and sideways. \n\nif dealer gamma is **negative**, they become gas pedals\u2014they have to chase the market higher when it goes up and panic-sell when it drops, turning a normal pullback into a full-scale waterfall."
